  "offerings": [
    {
      "uuid": "f1000000000000000000000000000001",
      "name": "Secure Government VM",
      "type": "Marketplace.Basic",
      "state": 2,
      "shared": true,
      "billable": true,
      "category_uuid": "d1000000000000000000000000000001",
      "customer_uuid": "b1000000000000000000000000000001",
      "description": "Government-certified virtual machines with security controls and audit logging",
      "plugin_options": {
        "service_provider_can_create_offering_user": true
      },
      "getting_started": "## Getting Started with Secure Government VM\n\n### Security Requirements\n1. **Use government-issued SSH keys only**\n2. All access is logged and audited\n3. MFA is required for console access\n\n### Connection\n```\nssh -i ~/.ssh/gov_key user@<vm-ip>\n```\n\n### Compliance\n- All VMs are ISO 27001 certified\n- Audit logs are retained for 7 years\n- Data residency: Estonia (EU)\n\nContact security@gov.cloud for compliance questions."
    },
    {
      "uuid": "f1000000000000000000000000000002",
      "name": "GDPR-Compliant Object Storage",
      "type": "Marketplace.Basic",
      "state": 2,
      "shared": true,
      "billable": true,
      "category_uuid": "d1000000000000000000000000000002",
      "customer_uuid": "b1000000000000000000000000000001",
      "description": "Encrypted object storage with GDPR compliance and data residency guarantees",
      "plugin_options": {
        "service_provider_can_create_offering_user": true
      },
      "getting_started": "## Getting Started with GDPR-Compliant Storage\n\n### Access Configuration\n1. Generate access credentials from the dashboard\n2. Configure your S3 client:\n   ```\n   aws configure --profile gov-storage\n   ```\n\n### GDPR Features\n- **Encryption**: AES-256 at rest, TLS 1.3 in transit\n- **Data Residency**: All data stored in EU\n- **Right to Erasure**: Automated deletion workflows available\n\n### Usage\n```\naws s3 cp file.txt s3://your-bucket/ --profile gov-storage\n```"
    },
    {
      "uuid": "f1000000000000000000000000000003",
      "name": "Managed PostgreSQL",
      "type": "Marketplace.Basic",
      "state": 2,
      "shared": true,
      "billable": true,
      "category_uuid": "d1000000000000000000000000000003",
      "customer_uuid": "b1000000000000000000000000000001",
      "description": "Managed PostgreSQL with automated backups and compliance auditing",
      "plugin_options": {
        "service_provider_can_create_offering_user": true
      },
      "getting_started": "## Getting Started with Managed PostgreSQL\n\n### Connection\n```\npsql -h <db-host> -U <username> -d <database>\n```\n\n### Features\n- **Automated Backups**: Daily at 02:00 UTC, 30-day retention\n- **Point-in-Time Recovery**: Available within retention period\n- **Audit Logging**: All queries logged for compliance\n\n### Best Practices\n1. Use connection pooling (PgBouncer included)\n2. Enable SSL for all connections\n3. Use read replicas for reporting queries"
    },
    {
      "uuid": "f1000000000000000000000000000010",
      "name": "Secure Kubernetes Cluster",
      "type": "Support.OfferingTemplate",
      "state": 2,
      "shared": true,
      "billable": true,
      "category_uuid": "d1000000000000000000000000000004",
